---
23:| 1 | bell cupola on the ridge (base through the roof, open belfry, cap) | 16..19 | 11..18 (+finial 19) | 13..16 |
37:| 4 | steeple tower (rises from the front of the nave, face flush with the gable) | 51..54 | 8..18 | 9..12 |
38:| 4 | spire (tower-cap) + finial | 51..54 | 19..24 (+25..26) | 9..12 |
68:| 4 church nave | steep front gable | `church` is a stave preset (wrong): use `cottage` with `ridgeAxis: z`, `front: n`, palette `slate`, verge `calcite` (white barge board) | along z at x 52..53, z 8..18 | eaves y 8 (x 48 / x 57), ridge y 12 | 1 | keep the tower x 51..54 z 8..12 from y 8 up; trusses `stripped_spruce_log` (scissor/king post open to the nave) |
69:| 4 spire | tall pyramid/cone | `tower-cap`, material `slate`, finial `lightning_rod` + a cross (spruce fence) y 25..26 | apex over x 52..53 z 10..11 | ring y 18 (calcite slab cornice proud 1, x 50..55 z 8..13), apex y 24 | 1 | the steeple is what the village below sees |
